      "text": "There are three types of real numbers: rational, irrational, and complex. The quadratic formula yields that all three of $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are irrational, and since a cubic root of a rational number is either irrational or rational, then $abc$ is either irrational or rational. It follows then that $ab + ac + bc$ is irrational, and thus it is either $\\boxed{4}$ or $\\boxed{-4}$. The answer is -4",
